<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Hardened Runtime is required for notarisation, and it revokes several
      capabilities unless they are asked for back. Only one is asked for here.

      Microphone: the whole point of the app. Without this entitlement the
      hardened runtime blocks capture before TCC is ever consulted.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
      Deliberately NOT requested:

      - App Sandbox. Sandboxing would break the global CGEventTap (there is no
        entitlement that restores it outside the App Store) and cut off
        ~/Documents, where WhisperKit keeps its weights.
      - allow-unsigned-executable-memory / allow-jit. Core ML loads compiled
        .mlmodelc artefacts as data, not as code. Adding these weakens the
        runtime for nothing; if a future engine genuinely needs them, that
        should be a deliberate, tested change.
      - disable-library-validation. yaz loads no third-party plug-ins.
      - Apple Events. yaz drives nothing through AppleScript.

      Watching the hotkey and pasting the transcript need no entitlement at
      all: they are governed by TCC (Accessibility and Input Monitoring), which
      the user grants at runtime.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
